1
00:00:26,194 --> 00:00:27,894
not a special human being,

2
00:00:27,994 --> 00:00:31,054
but I don't want to see it.

3
00:00:31,934 --> 00:00:35,934
The blue sky is bright, and
I'm looking forward to it.

4
00:00:36,874 --> 00:00:38,691
I'm looking forward to it in a little bit.

5
00:00:41,414 --> 00:00:44,894
I'm looking forward to it.

6
00:00:46,934 --> 00:00:48,463
I'm looking forward to it.

7
00:00:58,694 --> 00:01:01,971
Hai. Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

8
00:01:02,054 --> 00:01:04,031
Yeah. Yeah.

9
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:05,714
Yolta, Ima!

10
00:01:07,594 --> 00:01:08,535
Kyoumamaaakaaka!

11
00:01:09,234 --> 00:01:11,194
Halanfancho konoomori!

12
00:01:11,514 --> 00:01:14,314
Itsmoka so many tsukure!

13
00:01:14,554 --> 00:01:17,114
Sanja karan, sigamae!

14
00:01:17,314 --> 00:01:19,574
Kibi wo shinji te!

15
00:01:20,174 --> 00:01:22,554
Mayoobu te, naayamu te!

16
00:01:22,934 --> 00:01:25,294
Wanai naanara ikumou!

17
00:01:33,094 --> 00:01:34,565
It's all coming together.

18
00:01:35,074 --> 00:01:37,251
Tachibana's charm skill has proven useful.

19
00:01:37,334 --> 00:01:38,981
I barely had to do anything.

20
00:01:41,194 --> 00:01:43,194
So what exactly did you do to her?

21
00:01:43,374 --> 00:01:45,271
I boosted the power of her charm skill.

22
00:01:45,354 --> 00:01:49,471
Just enough to make it go a bit haywire,
which so happened to weaken the hero.

23
00:01:49,554 --> 00:01:51,654
Two birds with one stone? By now,

24
00:01:51,774 --> 00:01:55,211
the kingdom should be utterly overwhelmed
trying to quell the riots in the capital.

25
00:01:55,294 --> 00:01:58,591
Providing us with the opportunity to
have the humans destroy themselves.

26
00:01:58,674 --> 00:02:00,114
That is totally twisted!

27
00:02:00,414 --> 00:02:01,244
Head made!

28
00:02:01,327 --> 00:02:02,157
Emergency!

29
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,751
All communications with the troops
advancing on the capital have been cut off!

30
00:02:04,834 --> 00:02:06,331
Are you saying they were wiped out?

31
00:02:06,414 --> 00:02:10,414
Actually, it would seem they've all
gone back to their normal lives.

32
00:02:10,754 --> 00:02:14,225
Our scouts say they're now
plowing fields completely naked.

33
00:02:14,374 --> 00:02:15,334
Why naked?

34
00:02:15,654 --> 00:02:17,091
That point remains unclear.

35
00:02:17,174 --> 00:02:21,998
However, we can confirm that they've lost
all their memories of the last few days.

36
00:02:22,274 --> 00:02:26,531
How could there be a skill that can instantly
dispel the heroes charms on hundreds?

37
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:27,555
It's impossible.

38
00:02:27,934 --> 00:02:29,731
I don't get what the big deal is.

39
00:02:29,814 --> 00:02:31,391
What do you think would happen if all our

40
00:02:31,474 --> 00:02:33,791
charmed hostages made
an advance on the enemy,

41
00:02:33,874 --> 00:02:36,891
only to have their charms dispelled
moments after they reached them?

42
00:02:36,974 --> 00:02:38,531
Well, it'd make the hostages useless,

43
00:02:38,614 --> 00:02:41,971
which would defeat the whole reason
why we're here in the first place.

44
00:02:42,054 --> 00:02:43,466
Wait, that's really bad!

45
00:02:43,874 --> 00:02:44,704
We can't take it!

46
00:02:44,787 --> 00:02:45,811
No, this isn't happening.

47
00:02:45,894 --> 00:02:49,751
All those peeled potatoes, mop floors,
and cobbled shoes can't be for nothing.

48
00:02:49,834 --> 00:02:53,531
It took an entire year of working myself
to the bone just to become headmaid!

49
00:02:53,614 --> 00:02:57,491
All the while patiently gathering information
so I could craft the perfect plan.

50
00:02:57,574 --> 00:02:59,611
And yet somehow I miss
the one human in the

51
00:02:59,694 --> 00:03:01,671
entire kingdom who can undo mind control?

52
00:03:01,754 --> 00:03:02,872
Who even does that?

53
00:03:03,514 --> 00:03:04,954
This is really bad!

54
00:03:05,274 --> 00:03:06,862
This is really, really bad!

55
00:03:06,974 --> 00:03:08,231
What are you gonna do?

56
00:03:08,314 --> 00:03:09,144
This is really sad!

57
00:03:09,227 --> 00:03:10,411
There's no use fighting it.

58
00:03:10,494 --> 00:03:12,911
We'll abandon the kingdom
falls to charm strategy.

59
00:03:12,994 --> 00:03:15,571
Oh, so does that mean you'll
have some kind of backup plan?

60
00:03:15,654 --> 00:03:16,484
You know what?

61
00:03:16,567 --> 00:03:17,472
Screw it, honestly.

62
00:03:20,274 --> 00:03:22,862
How about we just blow
up the whole kingdom?

63
00:03:24,994 --> 00:03:27,194
Hey, Iki, what is this place?

64
00:03:27,494 --> 00:03:30,731
This chamber is where the kingdom
stores its strongest weapons.

65
00:03:30,814 --> 00:03:31,644
Princess,

66
00:03:31,727 --> 00:03:33,671
as much as I regret
that it's come to this,

67
00:03:33,754 --> 00:03:37,511
due to unforeseen interference, we've
been forced to abandon our original plan.

68
00:03:37,594 --> 00:03:40,674
The only path left to us
is to use our last resort.

69
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:42,084
Huh?

70
00:03:42,167 --> 00:03:45,591
You're seeing one plan failed and now
we're already down to our last resort?

71
00:03:45,674 --> 00:03:48,151
Sounds like it was a pretty
stupid plan to begin with.

72
00:03:48,234 --> 00:03:52,731
I'd prefer, Your Highness, to see it as
a sign of how desperate our situation is.

73
00:03:52,814 --> 00:03:57,751
Regardless, I'm not comfortable using the
Kingdom's defenses to achieve my own ends.

74
00:03:57,834 --> 00:04:00,775
Yet you're fine with
half-measures, Your Highness.

75
00:04:01,394 --> 00:04:04,394
You've borne the weight of
so much all by yourself.

76
00:04:04,674 --> 00:04:08,954
The power behind that door is yours
to take by right, don't you think?

77
00:04:12,474 --> 00:04:14,934
Remember that suffocating lonely world?

78
00:04:15,434 --> 00:04:17,905
Do you truly miss your life in the castle?

79
00:04:18,814 --> 00:04:20,234
But the seal...

80
00:04:20,934 --> 00:04:23,494
It requires two royal family members.

81
00:04:23,694 --> 00:04:25,812
There's no need to worry about that.

82
00:04:28,814 --> 00:04:32,234
Let's not forget, you've also
been touched by the goddess.

83
00:04:33,414 --> 00:04:35,834
Come on, you too, hero. Huh?

84
00:04:36,134 --> 00:04:38,663
Oh, sorry, I haven't
really been listening.

85
00:04:38,914 --> 00:04:40,174
Remember what I said?

86
00:04:40,394 --> 00:04:41,923
You wanted to be stronger.

87
00:04:42,234 --> 00:04:45,469
And I told you that I could
teach you a way to do that.

88
00:04:52,194 --> 00:04:53,811
We have what we need.

89
00:04:53,894 --> 00:04:56,074
So we can finally defeat Jinguji!

90
00:04:57,434 --> 00:04:58,264
Jinguji

91
00:05:04,814 --> 00:05:06,791
Manual, manual, manual.

92
00:05:06,874 --> 00:05:08,314
Found it!

93
00:05:09,214 --> 00:05:11,814
This doesn't feel right Why go so far?

94
00:05:12,014 --> 00:05:14,551
The last thing I want to do
is threat military action.

95
00:05:14,634 --> 00:05:15,971
Just to make a point to my father!

96
00:05:16,054 --> 00:05:17,371
All this time.

97
00:05:17,454 --> 00:05:19,925
And you still need it spelled out for you?

98
00:05:24,114 --> 00:05:27,408
Working for you this last
year hasn't been excruciating.

99
00:05:27,954 --> 00:05:29,831
That's why I'll save
her every second I spend

100
00:05:29,914 --> 00:05:33,032
turning your worthless
kingdom into a pile of rubble!

101
00:05:34,874 --> 00:05:37,851
Sounds like she's been
holding that back for a while?

102
00:05:37,934 --> 00:05:40,151
Hey, what do you want to
do with the other one?

103
00:05:40,234 --> 00:05:41,074
Oh the hero?

104
00:05:41,354 --> 00:05:45,236
I've got the perfect idea We plug
her in and use her as a battery.

105
00:05:45,514 --> 00:05:47,808
She has more than enough goddess power.

106
00:05:48,094 --> 00:05:48,924
Battery?

107
00:05:49,434 --> 00:05:51,493
Wait, are you guys talking about...

108
00:05:53,514 --> 00:05:56,014
Now then, Viz, it's time to wreck havoc!

109
00:05:56,234 --> 00:05:57,274
Switch on!

110
00:06:08,474 --> 00:06:09,534
What's going on?

111
00:06:09,914 --> 00:06:11,796
Jinguuji, what's that over there?

112
00:06:30,854 --> 00:06:32,774
Hey, Shen, what is that thing?

113
00:06:33,454 --> 00:06:35,336
Well, it's definitely something.

114
00:06:36,174 --> 00:06:37,974
Now is not the time for jokes.

115
00:06:38,534 --> 00:06:41,511
I get that you're upset, but
no need to bite my head off.

116
00:06:41,594 --> 00:06:42,535
How interesting.

117
00:06:42,974 --> 00:06:45,033
Do you see something, Interrogator?

118
00:06:45,394 --> 00:06:48,174
It's cute. That doesn't help. Oh, sorry.

119
00:06:48,394 --> 00:06:51,731
I meant to say it reminds me of
something I saw in a book long ago.

120
00:06:51,814 --> 00:06:54,873
A creature said to be this
kingdom's guardian deity.

121
00:06:54,974 --> 00:06:55,856
Guardian deity?

122
00:06:56,034 --> 00:06:58,651
You mean those weird forest
animals with the long ears?

123
00:06:58,734 --> 00:07:01,131
Big and intimidating
yet surprisingly cuddly?

124
00:07:01,214 --> 00:07:02,871
And they're fiercely
protective of believers

125
00:07:02,954 --> 00:07:05,778
and their faces can open
up and shoot out light?

126
00:07:06,334 --> 00:07:10,071
If it's designed after one of those
things, then maybe it showed up to help us.

127
00:07:10,154 --> 00:07:12,391
That's what guardian
deities are supposed to do.

128
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:15,834
It's possible that this
is a lucky omen. Whoa.

129
00:07:16,234 --> 00:07:17,587
Thanks, Guardian Deity.

130
00:07:17,774 --> 00:07:21,362
Actually, based on my experience,
I wouldn't get my hopes up.

131
00:07:34,874 --> 00:07:37,034
Case in point. Okay.

132
00:07:37,274 --> 00:07:39,871
I guess that's a never
mind on the thanks, then.

133
00:07:39,954 --> 00:07:40,784
What is this?

134
00:07:40,867 --> 00:07:44,834
Why would our guardian deity
turn against us? Your majesty?

135
00:07:45,094 --> 00:07:47,329
Can you tell us more about that thing?

136
00:07:47,574 --> 00:07:51,274
It is our kingdom's ancient
defense weapon, Mepon.

137
00:07:51,934 --> 00:07:55,194
A gift bestowed to us by our
goddess in ancient times.

138
00:07:55,354 --> 00:07:57,771
It can melt the enemy's heart
with its adorable design

139
00:07:57,854 --> 00:08:00,871
and melt fortifications with
its enormous beam weapon.

140
00:08:00,954 --> 00:08:04,778
Of course the goddess would make
something so completely asinine.

141
00:08:05,534 --> 00:08:09,591
But the guardian deity can only be activated
by two members of the royal family,

142
00:08:09,674 --> 00:08:11,071
each bearing a holy crest?

143
00:08:11,154 --> 00:08:15,911
How could this be then it has to be
Tachibana and the princess are behind this?

144
00:08:15,994 --> 00:08:21,691
Tachibana so any idea how we take it down?

145
00:08:21,774 --> 00:08:23,371
What makes you think i'd know?

146
00:08:23,454 --> 00:08:26,731
Dang it this thing's got a
lot more kick than i thought!

147
00:08:26,814 --> 00:08:28,931
I'm gonna adjust it a bit!

148
00:08:29,014 --> 00:08:31,491
Don't you dare even think
about adjusting anything!

149
00:08:31,574 --> 00:08:34,891
You already missed the first shot and
messing with it will only make things work!

150
00:08:34,974 --> 00:08:35,804
Quit!

151
00:08:35,887 --> 00:08:38,361
I'm blinding, I'll hit
the next one for sure!

152
00:08:42,334 --> 00:08:43,814
It's powering up again!

153
00:08:44,134 --> 00:08:45,794
Your Majesty, please run!

154
00:08:51,714 --> 00:08:53,890
Jinkuchi, we need to get out of here!

155
00:08:53,974 --> 00:08:58,621
Schwarz, as an adult I can tell you we're
nothing if not complicated creatures.

156
00:08:58,914 --> 00:09:00,674
There's a darkness inside us.

157
00:09:00,894 --> 00:09:03,291
It touches everything, even love.

158
00:09:03,374 --> 00:09:06,391
A handsome face really does
make anything sound believable.

159
00:09:06,474 --> 00:09:08,650
I thought Tachibana was no different.

160
00:09:08,814 --> 00:09:10,932
However, I see now that I was wrong.

161
00:09:11,094 --> 00:09:13,371
The robot might look
embarrassingly stupid,

162
00:09:13,454 --> 00:09:17,042
but it is undoubtedly a vicious
and powerful killing machine.

163
00:09:17,714 --> 00:09:20,491
Tachibana would never unleash
something like that on purpose.

164
00:09:20,574 --> 00:09:22,131
So you're worried about him?

165
00:09:22,214 --> 00:09:23,851
It doesn't matter how I feel.

166
00:09:23,934 --> 00:09:26,346
Whoever's controlling the Guardian deity,

167
00:09:27,074 --> 00:09:29,314
it's my responsibility to stop it.

168
00:09:34,114 --> 00:09:38,071
Well, I'm not going to stand here and
let you take all the glory for yourself.

169
00:09:38,154 --> 00:09:38,994
Are you sure?

170
00:09:39,994 --> 00:09:43,811
You and I are the only ones in the castle
who can do anything against that robot.

171
00:09:43,894 --> 00:09:47,751
If we don't make a stand here and
now, it'll destroy the whole kingdom.

172
00:09:47,834 --> 00:09:49,246
Isn't that what this is?

173
00:09:50,274 --> 00:09:51,534
It's exactly that.

174
00:09:52,614 --> 00:09:54,496
Well, you can take it from here.

175
00:09:56,614 --> 00:10:00,311
Thing is, my supernatural strength
is tied to my proximity to Tachibana,

176
00:10:00,394 --> 00:10:01,276
who isn't here.

177
00:10:01,694 --> 00:10:03,106
So I won't be much help.

178
00:10:03,374 --> 00:10:04,711
Dude, you gotta be kidding me!

179
00:10:04,794 --> 00:10:06,091
You at least have a plan, right?

180
00:10:06,174 --> 00:10:08,871
Something that involves saving
everyone and not leaving me to die?

181
00:10:08,954 --> 00:10:10,191
I'm sorry, but I don't.

182
00:10:10,274 --> 00:10:11,611
What's the matter with you?!

183
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:14,591
Correct me if I'm wrong, but can't
his sword cut through anything?

184
00:10:14,674 --> 00:10:17,271
So, it stands to reason that it
could also cut through the beam.

185
00:10:17,354 --> 00:10:19,648
That's a good idea, let's go with that.

186
00:10:20,014 --> 00:10:21,491
Can we talk about this first?

187
00:10:21,574 --> 00:10:23,951
A slapped-together plan
cannot be our best option!

188
00:10:24,034 --> 00:10:25,971
If you've got a better one, I'm all ears.

189
00:10:26,054 --> 00:10:28,071
We're kinda out of time to brainstorm.

190
00:10:28,154 --> 00:10:29,774
Good luck. Don't die.

191
00:10:30,474 --> 00:10:31,304
No!

192
00:10:31,414 --> 00:10:32,244
One!

193
00:10:32,327 --> 00:10:36,108
And remember we're all counting on
you to make sure we don't end up dead.

194
00:10:38,254 --> 00:10:40,414
This way please remain calm.

195
00:11:06,494 --> 00:11:10,788
Would you look at that guess it did
work nice you actually did something.

196
00:11:13,574 --> 00:11:17,191
Now I just have to do the same thing
for the next one all right easy peasy.

197
00:11:17,274 --> 00:11:18,991
Because if I don't stop
it then you're gonna

198
00:11:19,074 --> 00:11:21,674
die and I'm gonna die
everyone's gonna die.

199
00:11:22,294 --> 00:11:25,774
You're starting to sound like
a real hero no one asked you.

200
00:11:29,074 --> 00:11:29,911
Congratulations, humans.

201
00:11:29,994 --> 00:11:31,582
You're all still breathing.

202
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,074
Whose voice is that?

203
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,711
Did it come from inside the Watson?

204
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:36,088
That sounded familiar.

205
00:11:36,734 --> 00:11:39,174
As a reward, I'll share with you my name.

206
00:11:39,694 --> 00:11:44,054
I am this, the incomparably skilled,
top officer for the great Demon Lord.

207
00:11:44,274 --> 00:11:47,531
And when I'm through with you, I'm gonna
take your corpses as soon as you...

208
00:11:47,614 --> 00:11:48,444
Oh, it's her.

209
00:11:48,527 --> 00:11:52,031
If you're one of the Demon Lord's officers,
then there's no need to hold back.

210
00:11:52,114 --> 00:11:54,131
I'm gonna cut you into tiny little pieces!

211
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:55,731
Really intimidating, Sparts.

212
00:11:55,814 --> 00:11:56,644
You're doing awesome.

213
00:11:56,727 --> 00:11:58,291
You totally got this, buddy.

214
00:11:58,374 --> 00:11:59,550
Can it, both of you!

215
00:12:00,654 --> 00:12:03,360
You talk a lot for a
glorified side character.

216
00:12:03,554 --> 00:12:06,319
It's gonna be fun watching
you eat those words.

217
00:12:06,474 --> 00:12:09,231
Wait, am I losing it or can she
hear us from inside that thing?

218
00:12:09,314 --> 00:12:11,051
I'm guessing it's those stupid ears.

219
00:12:11,134 --> 00:12:12,605
What are you waiting for?

220
00:12:12,754 --> 00:12:15,891
It's not like I've got your precious
hero in here with me or anything.

221
00:12:15,974 --> 00:12:16,814
Oh, wait.

222
00:12:17,594 --> 00:12:19,594
She's using Tachibana as a shield?

223
00:12:20,014 --> 00:12:21,779
Let him go, you dirty cowards!

224
00:12:21,994 --> 00:12:23,551
Now, let's not be so harsh.

225
00:12:23,634 --> 00:12:25,931
How else could she
level the playing field?

226
00:12:26,014 --> 00:12:27,511
She's just a child, after all.

227
00:12:27,594 --> 00:12:30,011
Such a clever plan, too!

228
00:12:30,094 --> 00:12:31,291
Did you come up with it yourself?

229
00:12:31,374 --> 00:12:33,691
Oh, that is it.

230
00:12:33,774 --> 00:12:36,011
Do you want to die for us?

231
00:12:36,094 --> 00:12:37,374
It's so gorgeous.

232
00:12:39,554 --> 00:12:41,711
Why did you have to go
and provoke her like that?

233
00:12:41,794 --> 00:12:42,651
Good.

234
00:12:42,734 --> 00:12:45,654
Next part's on you. Get ready! Wait.

235
00:12:51,914 --> 00:12:53,114
That felt good.

236
00:12:58,334 --> 00:13:00,351
Did I vaporize Four Eyes and his friends?

237
00:13:00,434 --> 00:13:01,264
Of course not!

238
00:13:01,347 --> 00:13:02,371
You missed, you idiot!

239
00:13:02,454 --> 00:13:05,231
Now they're getting away because
of your gross incompetence!

240
00:13:05,314 --> 00:13:07,211
Get your act together and keep firing!

241
00:13:07,294 --> 00:13:11,351
You should've kept blasting from the
beginning instead of trading banter with them!

242
00:13:11,434 --> 00:13:13,031
Mepon isn't built to rapid fire.

243
00:13:13,114 --> 00:13:14,691
It has to cool down for
a while before it can

244
00:13:14,774 --> 00:13:16,671
shoot off another one of
its adorable deathbeds.

245
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:19,091
That's why have you been
wasting shots this whole time?

246
00:13:19,174 --> 00:13:20,115
Get off my back!

247
00:13:20,254 --> 00:13:22,151
At least I'm trying to keep
them distracted with witty

248
00:13:22,234 --> 00:13:24,711
conversations so they don't
notice we have a weakness.

249
00:13:24,794 --> 00:13:26,531
But when you say witty conversation,

250
00:13:26,614 --> 00:13:29,831
are you talking about the part where you
revealed to them exactly where the hero is?

251
00:13:29,914 --> 00:13:33,451
Did you think that four-eyed barbarian
kept goading you because I was funny?

252
00:13:33,534 --> 00:13:36,471
Quit moaning and stop him before
he's close enough to attack!

253
00:13:36,554 --> 00:13:39,331
Well, if you stop criticizing
me for five seconds,

254
00:13:39,414 --> 00:13:42,238
then maybe I can get back
to trying to kill him!

255
00:13:45,374 --> 00:13:46,474
Get ready to land.

256
00:13:46,634 --> 00:13:47,464
This is all you!

257
00:13:53,914 --> 00:13:55,326
Everything feels broken!

258
00:13:55,514 --> 00:13:58,711
Now that she's lost line of sight,
she'll stop firing on the castle,

259
00:13:58,794 --> 00:14:00,991
giving us a chance to
evacuate the capital?

260
00:14:01,074 --> 00:14:03,956
and leaving an opening to
launch a counterattack.

261
00:14:04,294 --> 00:14:06,794
It seems Mehpon can't fire continuously.

262
00:14:07,214 --> 00:14:10,651
There was a noticeable delay
between the first and second shots.

263
00:14:10,734 --> 00:14:13,151
I suspect that Vizd
attempting all that banter was

264
00:14:13,234 --> 00:14:15,371
her trying to keep us from
noticing its weakness.

265
00:14:15,454 --> 00:14:19,371
But thanks to that, we now know
Tachibana is being kept inside the robot.

266
00:14:19,454 --> 00:14:21,748
We can use this time to close in on it.

267
00:14:21,894 --> 00:14:26,631
My strength will return if we get within
range, and once my power's back, we attack.

268
00:14:26,714 --> 00:14:27,773
Got any questions?

269
00:14:27,934 --> 00:14:28,791
Just one little thing.

270
00:14:28,874 --> 00:14:32,227
Are you okay with me stealing
that got me questions line?

271
00:14:32,314 --> 00:14:33,971
I want to add it to my
list of cool one-liners

272
00:14:34,054 --> 00:14:36,011
to use at some point
during my next adventure.

273
00:14:36,094 --> 00:14:37,271
There's no time for this.

274
00:14:37,354 --> 00:14:38,707
The next shot's coming.

275
00:14:38,954 --> 00:14:39,854
Hey, Jinguji!

276
00:14:40,274 --> 00:14:42,568
I thought maybe a croco-dog would help.

277
00:14:49,354 --> 00:14:50,184
What the?

278
00:14:50,974 --> 00:14:52,694
Why am I floating?

279
00:14:53,414 --> 00:14:55,034
Why even is this place?

280
00:14:55,654 --> 00:14:57,894
Where was I before I woke up here?

281
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:04,852
They sure love their giant
laser beams in this world.

282
00:15:05,374 --> 00:15:08,094
Am I in the middle of a battle right now?

283
00:15:15,374 --> 00:15:16,204
Jinguji...

284
00:15:20,154 --> 00:15:20,984
Nappan!

285
00:15:21,334 --> 00:15:22,164
Master?

286
00:15:23,934 --> 00:15:25,054
Tsukasa Jinguji,

287
00:15:25,314 --> 00:15:27,911
on behalf of myself and the
school I'm happy to present

288
00:15:27,994 --> 00:15:30,631
you with this award for
your achievements in Kendo.

289
00:15:30,714 --> 00:15:33,251
He's so awesome! I can't
even make the team!

290
00:15:33,334 --> 00:15:35,431
I heard that he can pretty
much do anything he tries.

291
00:15:35,514 --> 00:15:37,161
Man, I wish I was that cool!

292
00:15:50,154 --> 00:15:51,754
This is so stupid!

293
00:15:52,014 --> 00:15:54,251
What idiot can a sword that
can cut through laser beam?

294
00:15:54,334 --> 00:15:56,091
These buildings be
frustratingly effective.

295
00:15:56,174 --> 00:15:58,271
Do we have anything that can counter it?

296
00:15:58,354 --> 00:16:00,374
If I wasn't made for melee combat,

297
00:16:00,654 --> 00:16:03,091
if they close the gap, then
it's basically useless!

298
00:16:03,174 --> 00:16:06,311
Just hit him with whatever power
he used to break me out of jail!

299
00:16:06,394 --> 00:16:09,111
That spell takes more time
than we have to prepare.

300
00:16:09,194 --> 00:16:12,091
Can you do anything right now
besides being a loud mountain man?

301
00:16:12,174 --> 00:16:14,771
My skills are better suited
for covert operations.

302
00:16:14,854 --> 00:16:17,111
We need to figure out
something fast or we're hosed!

303
00:16:17,194 --> 00:16:19,031
If they're able to deflect my next attack,

304
00:16:19,114 --> 00:16:21,511
they'll be dead on top of me
and it's bye-bye bunnybot!

305
00:16:21,594 --> 00:16:22,424
Right,

306
00:16:22,507 --> 00:16:25,611
to keep that from happening, I'll put every
ounce of power we have into this shot!

307
00:16:25,694 --> 00:16:28,400
You fool, that's not a
plan to start to death!

308
00:16:28,514 --> 00:16:31,491
I can't allow it to set up a reaction
too big for Mepoam to get attacked!

309
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:33,011
Shut up, I know what I'm doing!

310
00:16:33,094 --> 00:16:34,194
Now here I go!

311
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:35,824
Shut up!

312
00:16:37,634 --> 00:16:38,464
What happened?

313
00:16:38,547 --> 00:16:39,377
Is it busted?

314
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:40,290
What's going on?

315
00:16:40,373 --> 00:16:41,308
Is everything alright?

316
00:16:42,994 --> 00:16:43,824
The heck?

317
00:16:44,094 --> 00:16:46,031
Everything's shutting
down all of a sudden!

318
00:16:46,114 --> 00:16:48,474
Shutting down? But how? What is this?

319
00:16:49,574 --> 00:16:50,671
We're almost there.

320
00:16:50,754 --> 00:16:52,751
We'll go under it and
attack from the other side.

321
00:16:52,834 --> 00:16:55,111
It won't be able to hit us with that beam.

322
00:16:55,194 --> 00:16:57,134
Look, Jinguji! Above us!

323
00:17:00,974 --> 00:17:05,092
At least you're smart enough to
change up your tactics at close range.

324
00:17:05,374 --> 00:17:08,291
But not smart enough to
take me on, you rotten brat.

325
00:17:08,374 --> 00:17:10,074
Oh, sorry for being a brat!

326
00:17:11,214 --> 00:17:12,774
Tachibana, is that you?

327
00:17:13,514 --> 00:17:14,394
Uh-huh!

328
00:17:15,114 --> 00:17:15,944
I'm cold!

329
00:17:17,454 --> 00:17:18,471
Meifu, it's broken!

330
00:17:18,554 --> 00:17:20,651
I promise it totally wasn't my fault!

331
00:17:20,734 --> 00:17:23,471
It got all dark and scary and
started moving when I found it!

332
00:17:23,554 --> 00:17:24,384
Now I won't even listen!

333
00:17:24,467 --> 00:17:26,140
Someone's going on a rampage!

334
00:17:26,354 --> 00:17:27,184
Rampage?

335
00:17:27,267 --> 00:17:29,111
Is this because I pushed you too hard?

336
00:17:29,194 --> 00:17:30,253
Forgive me, Meifu!

337
00:17:30,374 --> 00:17:31,550
I didn't mean Meifu.

338
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,874
I was referring to the hero.

339
00:17:35,074 --> 00:17:35,904
Huh?!

340
00:17:35,987 --> 00:17:37,211
It's okay, Tachibana.

341
00:17:37,294 --> 00:17:38,529
I'm here to save you!

342
00:17:38,674 --> 00:17:40,231
You'll be safe in there for now.

343
00:17:40,314 --> 00:17:41,351
I'll get you out soon.

344
00:17:41,434 --> 00:17:42,264
Don't worry!

345
00:17:42,774 --> 00:17:44,654
Okay, uh, why would I want out?

346
00:17:44,914 --> 00:17:47,271
I finally got my hands on some real power.

347
00:17:47,354 --> 00:17:48,411
Why should I give it up?

348
00:17:48,494 --> 00:17:50,431
Why go back to the way I was before?

349
00:17:50,514 --> 00:17:53,051
Is it me, or is there
something off with him?

350
00:17:53,134 --> 00:17:54,663
You listen to me, Jinguuji.

351
00:17:55,654 --> 00:17:57,714
I will defeat you! Why?

352
00:17:58,334 --> 00:17:59,914
I came here to save you!

353
00:18:00,174 --> 00:18:02,350
Does it look like I need to be saved?

354
00:18:02,714 --> 00:18:07,596
Then again, you always have to be the hero,
reminding everyone how perfect you are.

355
00:18:08,034 --> 00:18:09,271
Women always adore you,

356
00:18:09,354 --> 00:18:11,771
even though you treat them like
something that crawled out of the sewer!

357
00:18:11,854 --> 00:18:14,471
and bosses love you because you're
perfect at everything you do!

358
00:18:14,554 --> 00:18:18,274
And that's why I friggin'
hate you! Hate you!

359
00:18:19,074 --> 00:18:21,574
Did you see that coming? I did not.

360
00:18:21,854 --> 00:18:23,431
You guys have a fight or something?

361
00:18:23,514 --> 00:18:25,871
No, I thought things were fine between us.

362
00:18:25,954 --> 00:18:26,784
Shut up, Jungle Jim!

363
00:18:26,867 --> 00:18:28,371
You don't understand
what I've gone through!

364
00:18:28,454 --> 00:18:30,351
Maybe you're too perfect
to have repressed emotions,

365
00:18:30,434 --> 00:18:32,787
but I know I'm not for those both of us!

366
00:18:34,234 --> 00:18:38,471
I can feel this power flowing through me,
telling me to crush everything in my path.

367
00:18:38,554 --> 00:18:41,436
For the first time in my
life, I feel invincible!

368
00:18:41,554 --> 00:18:44,871
I didn't realize anyone still
used that kind of cheesy dialogue.

369
00:18:44,954 --> 00:18:47,891
I'm not sure Tachibana would
appreciate hearing that from you.

370
00:18:47,974 --> 00:18:49,551
This is getting out of hand.

371
00:18:49,634 --> 00:18:51,611
Why don't we just bust
in and break him loose?

372
00:18:51,694 --> 00:18:55,311
We're close enough now that your
strength should be back, right?

373
00:18:55,394 --> 00:18:56,224
About that.

374
00:18:56,307 --> 00:18:59,831
In spite of being closer, I'm afraid
my strength still hasn't returned.

375
00:18:59,914 --> 00:19:00,744
What?!

376
00:19:00,827 --> 00:19:02,151
You mean now I have to
fight this thing alone?!

377
00:19:02,234 --> 00:19:04,571
And how exactly do you expect
me to do that, genius?!

378
00:19:04,654 --> 00:19:09,595
All this time, I thought my strength was
tied directly to my proximity to Tachibana.

379
00:19:09,754 --> 00:19:10,584
Huh.

380
00:19:10,667 --> 00:19:12,131
The menu hasn't popped
up to explain anything.

381
00:19:12,214 --> 00:19:13,174
What's going on?

382
00:19:17,874 --> 00:19:19,286
Tachibana, listen to me!

383
00:19:20,154 --> 00:19:23,291
Sure, I'm popular with women and
bosses, but those are separate issues.

384
00:19:23,374 --> 00:19:25,231
Why are you only upset about it now?

385
00:19:25,314 --> 00:19:27,726
Probably because you say stuff like that.

386
00:19:28,354 --> 00:19:29,184
Why?

387
00:19:29,267 --> 00:19:30,394
Oh, I'll tell you why.

388
00:19:32,514 --> 00:19:34,434
You never compliment me!

389
00:19:36,174 --> 00:19:37,004
Huh? Huh?

390
00:19:37,254 --> 00:19:38,914
You have no idea, do you?

391
00:19:39,054 --> 00:19:43,391
How people have treated me just for being
around you, let alone being your friend.

392
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:46,356
Looking at me like a poo
trailing off a goldfish.

393
00:19:46,474 --> 00:19:51,062
That's barely the tip of the iceberg of
crappy opinions people have had of me!

394
00:19:51,554 --> 00:19:53,051
And you're not any better!

395
00:19:53,134 --> 00:19:55,154
Not one bit! Me?

396
00:19:55,754 --> 00:19:58,091
We've been best friends
almost our entire lives,

397
00:19:58,174 --> 00:20:00,471
and you've never given
me a compliment once!

398
00:20:00,554 --> 00:20:03,051
Even now, I finally managed
to get stronger than you,

399
00:20:03,134 --> 00:20:06,371
and you still haven't said
anything nice about it to me!

400
00:20:06,454 --> 00:20:09,011
You need to do something quick
or he's going to kill us!

401
00:20:09,094 --> 00:20:10,506
I don't know what to do.

402
00:20:10,894 --> 00:20:14,411
He told you straight up that he wanted to
be brave, so just give him a compliment!

403
00:20:14,494 --> 00:20:15,771
Just give a compliment, huh?

404
00:20:15,854 --> 00:20:17,442
That should be easy, right?

405
00:20:19,534 --> 00:20:21,774
Hey, Tachibana! What? What is it?

406
00:20:21,914 --> 00:20:25,134
I think you're super cool, bruh.

407
00:20:26,214 --> 00:20:28,391
You said that because you
feel like you have to!

408
00:20:28,474 --> 00:20:29,434
This is bad!

409
00:20:30,794 --> 00:20:31,624
Shikuchi!

410
00:20:37,134 --> 00:20:38,971
Since Japan has lots of earthquakes,

411
00:20:39,054 --> 00:20:41,271
Japanese doors are built to
take a lot of punishment.

412
00:20:41,354 --> 00:20:42,766
And look, not a scratch.

413
00:20:42,934 --> 00:20:45,351
Never would have thought
to use one like a shield!

414
00:20:45,434 --> 00:20:46,971
Now you've taken it too far!

415
00:20:47,054 --> 00:20:48,411
This isn't a game, Tachibana!

416
00:20:48,494 --> 00:20:49,371
This is dangerous!

417
00:20:49,454 --> 00:20:52,591
If I were anyone else, I'd be—
Well, good thing you're not, huh?

418
00:20:52,674 --> 00:20:55,471
Everyone's always telling you
how amazing and cool you are!

419
00:20:55,554 --> 00:20:56,384
But not me!

420
00:20:56,574 --> 00:21:00,398
They sing your praises and never
say a single kind word about me!

421
00:21:00,494 --> 00:21:02,731
But you're the worst out of all of them!

422
00:21:02,814 --> 00:21:05,191
It's like you can't find a
single good thing about me!

423
00:21:05,274 --> 00:21:06,494
and that hurts!

424
00:21:07,534 --> 00:21:10,611
I just want a tenth of the
positive attention you get.

425
00:21:10,694 --> 00:21:13,151
I'm sorry you feel that way,
and I'm trying to understand,

426
00:21:13,234 --> 00:21:15,491
but I can't do it when
you're throwing a tantrum!

427
00:21:15,574 --> 00:21:16,404
Shut up!

428
00:21:16,487 --> 00:21:17,931
Don't you think I know that already?

429
00:21:18,014 --> 00:21:20,779
I'd find some better way
to do this if I could.

430
00:21:21,174 --> 00:21:24,231
I understand that I'm being
childish and self-centered,

431
00:21:24,314 --> 00:21:29,254
and I realize it's not right, but sometimes
I don't know how to be a grown-up.

432
00:21:29,834 --> 00:21:30,714
I'm not smart.

433
00:21:30,894 --> 00:21:31,951
I'm not attractive.

434
00:21:32,034 --> 00:21:33,331
I always need saving.

435
00:21:33,414 --> 00:21:35,874
There's nothing special about me!

436
00:21:36,794 --> 00:21:38,174
He really is hurting.

437
00:21:41,054 --> 00:21:43,571
That's why they called me
a trailing goldfish poo!

438
00:21:43,654 --> 00:21:46,531
Because they knew I could
never be what you are, Jinguji!

439
00:21:46,614 --> 00:21:48,911
So no matter how much
cuter or stronger I get,

440
00:21:48,994 --> 00:21:52,112
if I'm worthless to you, it
means I truly am nothing!

441
00:21:52,214 --> 00:21:54,351
This is what it always comes back to!

442
00:21:54,434 --> 00:21:58,846
The only thing in my life I can brag
about is having you for a best friend!

443
00:22:00,654 --> 00:22:04,242
And I'm sick of being someone
who has something that's wrong!

444
00:22:28,694 --> 00:22:30,274
Let's go!

445
00:22:34,494 --> 00:22:35,324
Let's go!

446
00:22:35,494 --> 00:22:36,354
Fabulous!

447
00:23:24,814 --> 00:23:26,214
Yeah!

448
00:23:36,574 --> 00:23:38,074
I will now read a letter.

449
00:23:38,254 --> 00:23:40,971
I have a question about that freaky
weird dog crocodile creature.

450
00:23:41,054 --> 00:23:42,431
Oh, you mean the Crocodog?

451
00:23:42,514 --> 00:23:44,231
Do you know what kind of sound it makes?

452
00:23:44,314 --> 00:23:45,196
Let's find out!

453
00:23:45,354 --> 00:23:47,451
Come on, make a sound for the audience!

454
00:23:47,534 --> 00:23:48,994
Come on, speak, speak!
